<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Brynner is a 63-year-old man with stage IVB adenocarcinoma of the left upper lobe on first-line pembrolizumab every 3 weeks (two cycles so far) and zoledronic acid every 12 weeks, who comes for his yearly preventive visit, timed before the respiratory virus season. The rash seen last week is fading with the triamcinolone cream, and the itching is much less; he has used cetirizine on three nights. He has had no new symptoms of immune-related side effects. His voice is stronger after the injection medialization and voice therapy, and he has begun rehearsing two hours a day; he hopes to rejoin the tour for a few performances a week next month. He saw the palliative care team four weeks ago and found it useful. He completed the health risk assessment before the visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Visit</td><td>Adult preventive visit</td></tr><tr><td>Active treatment</td><td>Pembrolizumab every 3 weeks; zoledronic acid every 12 weeks; vitamin D3 daily</td></tr><tr><td>Interval change</td><td>Rash fading on topical steroid; no other immune-related symptoms</td></tr><tr><td>Work</td><td>Rehearsing two hours a day; plans a graded return to the tour</td></tr><tr><td>Supports</td><td>Spouse, company manager, and the palliative care team</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Health risk assessment. Completed by the patient before the visit and reviewed during the visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Self-rated health</td><td>Good, apart from tiring by evening</td></tr><tr><td>Psychosocial</td><td>Worried about the future but coping; strong sense of purpose in returning to the stage; supportive spouse and company</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco</td><td>Former smoker; no tobacco for 12 years</td></tr><tr><td>Alcohol and drugs</td><td>A glass of wine two or three nights a week (AUDIT-C 2); no other drug use</td></tr><tr><td>Physical activity</td><td>Walks 30 minutes most days and does stage warm-ups</td></tr><tr><td>Nutrition</td><td>Eating well; weight stable at about 72 kg</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>About seven hours a night; itching woke him twice last week</td></tr><tr><td>Activities of daily living</td><td>Independent</td></tr><tr><td>Instrumental activities of daily living</td><td>Independent; company manager handles travel bookings</td></tr><tr><td>Home and travel safety</td><td>Smoke detectors at home; seat belt always; hotel rooms booked near elevators</td></tr><tr><td>Falls</td><td>None</td></tr><tr><td>Hearing and vision</td><td>Reading glasses; no hearing difficulty</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
