    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Adult preventive visit completed</content>. Health risk assessment reviewed and a written prevention plan given, adapted to active treatment for metastatic lung cancer: vaccines are the priority, and screening tests whose benefit takes years are deferred until the first response scan. Depression and alcohol screens negative. [S]<list><item>Influenza, PCV20, and recombinant zoster dose 1 today.</item><item>COVID-19 vaccine next week; RSV vaccine at the next visit.</item><item>Next preventive visit in one year.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Immune-related rash, grade 1, improving (L27.0)</content>. Fading with topical steroid; no blisters or mucosal involvement. [S]<list><item>Finish the two-week course of triamcinolone, then emollient alone.</item><item>Cetirizine as needed.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Stage IVB adenocarcinoma of the lung on pembrolizumab (C34.12)</content>. Two cycles given; no other immune-related events; preparing to return to work. [S]<list><item>Cycle 3 next week after the laboratory panel.</item><item>Response CT in about four weeks.</item><item>Palliative care follow-up next month.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Influenza vaccine, this season</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Inactivated vaccine given today; safe on checkpoint inhibitor therapy</td></tr><tr><td>Pneumococcal vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PCV20 given today; recommended once for all adults 50 and older</td></tr><tr><td>Recombinant zoster vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Dose 1 given today; dose 2 in two to six months</td></tr><tr><td>COVID-19 vaccine, this season</td><td>Due</td><td>Recommended; at his pharmacy next week, spaced from today&apos;s vaccines at his request</td></tr><tr><td>RSV vaccine</td><td>Due</td><td>Recommended at 60 to 74 for adults at increased risk, which his lung cancer confers; planned for the next visit</td></tr><tr><td>Tetanus, diphtheria, and pertussis booster</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Tdap six years ago</td></tr><tr><td>Colorectal cancer screening</td><td>Due</td><td>Recommended at 45 to 75; deferred by shared decision while he starts treatment for metastatic cancer; to be revisited after the first response scan</td></tr><tr><td>Prostate cancer screening</td><td>Declined</td><td>Individual decision at 55 to 69; after discussion he declined PSA testing while on cancer treatment</td></tr><tr><td>Lung cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>He has lung cancer and is followed with response imaging</td></tr><tr><td>Abdominal aortic aneurysm screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>One-time ultrasound for men 65 to 75 who have ever smoked; he is 63, and his staging CT showed a normal abdominal aorta</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis C and HIV screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>One-time screening for both done in the past, negative</td></tr><tr><td>Cholesterol screening and statin decision</td><td>Due</td><td>Deferred by shared decision while he starts treatment for metastatic cancer</td></tr><tr><td>Diabetes screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Glucose is checked before each pembrolizumab infusion; 94 to 104 mg/dL</td></tr><tr><td>Blood pressure screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>124/76 mmHg</td></tr><tr><td>Depression screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-2 score 1; PHQ-9 4 two weeks ago</td></tr><tr><td>Unhealthy alcohol use screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>AUDIT-C 2, below the risk threshold</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco use</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Former smoker; no tobacco for 12 years</td></tr><tr><td>Skin examination</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Rash fading; no suspicious lesions</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Influenza vaccine, 2026-2027 season; Pneumococcal conjugate vaccine PCV20, single dose; Recombinant zoster vaccine, dose 1 of 2 [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, lung cancer monograph (2026); Integration of Palliative Care Into Standard Oncology Care: American Society of Clinical Oncology Clinical Practice Guideline Update (2017); Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026); USPSTF A and B Recommendations (2026); Adult Immunization Schedule by Age (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Cycle 3 of pembrolizumab next week. COVID-19 vaccine at the pharmacy next week. Response CT in about four weeks. RSV vaccine and zoster dose 2 at later visits. Next preventive visit in one year. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

