    <code code="42348-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Advance directives"/>
    <title>Advance Care Planning</title>
    <text><paragraph>Voluntary advance care planning discussion of about 30 minutes, with his consent, building on the goals-of-care conversation with the palliative care team. We talked about what metastatic lung cancer can mean, that treatment aims to control it and help him live well for as long as possible rather than to cure it, and why it helps to plan ahead while he is well. He named a health care agent, who is recorded in the chart and not named here, and took a health care proxy form and a living will form home. He said what matters most to him is to keep working on the stage for as long as he can and to be told the truth plainly. He wants full cancer treatment now. He chose not to record other specific treatment preferences today. The plan will be revisited at the first response scan and at any change in his health. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>
